    {
      "id": "claim_e317edb131494479b71c1c0d3570d734",
      "statement": "A generation is everything a node derives from a deployment — compiled Worker configs, isolate pools, the Durable Object class registry, service-binding graph, asset resolvers, and cron schedule — and a node reaches it through a snapshot so a request that started on one generation finishes on it after adoption.",
